{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c771","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b07e-1184-7ee2-a636-22f940ee305b"},"sequence":531,"recorded_at":1780531400001057,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8a76739b-7cd3-4623-8bf5-9ad19ff6cfdd","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8a76739b-7cd3-4623-8bf5-9ad19ff6cfdd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8a76739b-7cd3-4623-8bf5-9ad19ff6cfdd"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b080-0b2d-7882-8d1b-7f10a69b55d1"},"task_id":"01a0b080-0b2d-7882-8d1b-7f10a69b55d1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b080-0b2d-7882-8d1b-7f10a69b55d1","chunk":"Read text file `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Clone Bundle Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-24z2b3)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/clonebundle`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1.\n5|The Story's FINAL leaf carries the `internal/traceability` registry\n6|bindings and re-pin; this file is the first-leaf clause record.\n7|\n8|## Why this package validates instead of canonicaljson\n9|\n10|The `canonicaljson` closed-shape registry keeps\n11|`rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows for\n12|`clone-raw-object-manifest`, `clone-capture-manifest`,\n13|`canonical-session`, and `canonical-event` 1.0.0, and that table's\n14|census pins every row. Replacing them would fork shape ownership, so\n15|this package is the validating owner: it reuses\n16|`canonicaljson.Canonicalize` (byte transform),\n17|`canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity` plus a local claim comparison\n18|(Blob Descriptors; never the attesting entry, per the provhost\n19|no-attestation bound),\n20|`sessadapter.DecodeTuple` (Environment Tuples),\n21|`environ.CheckExtensions` (extension keys),\n22|`scalar` (digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, paths),\n23|`hosttrust` (row-21 exclusion matchers), and\n24|`localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob` (blob install). No rule is\n25|reimplemented where a landed owner exists.\n26|\n27|## Clause map\n28|\n29|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n30||---|---|---|\n31|| 13.14.1 Raw Manifest closed envelope + self ID | `BuildRawObjectManifest`, `DecodeRawObjectManifest` | `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestRawManifestRefusals/decode` |\n32|| 13.14.1 RawObjectEntry class subset (no credential/auth/runtime/lock) | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries` | `TestRawManifestRefusals/build` (5 class rows) |\n33|| 13.14.1 sorted unique entries, total_bytes sum | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries` | `TestRawManifestRefusals` (unsorted, duplicate, total mismatch) |\n34|| 13.14.1 sanitized native key, never an AX Session ID | `SanitizeNativeKey` | `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer`, raw/capture/session/event refusal rows |\n35|| Row 21 exclusion allowlist at construction | `refuseExcludedMember` | `TestRawManifestExcludesTrustMaterial`, `TestCaptureManifestExcludesTrustMaterial` |\n36|| 13.14.1 CaptureItem 9-class vocabulary | `ValidCaptureClass`, `buildCaptureItem`, `decodeCaptureItem` | `TestCaptureClassVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestCaptureItemRefusals` |\n37|| 13.14.1 included/excluded content rule | `checkItemDisposition` | `TestCaptureItemRefusals` (6 content rows) |\n38|| 13.14.1 always-excluded classes never included | `alwaysExcludedClass` | `TestCaptureItemRefusals` (4 class rows) |\n39|| 13.14.1 exact excluded_classes | `excludedRowClasses`, `excludedClassesExact` | `TestExcludedClassesExactGate`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/decode` |\n40|| 13.14.1 core-derived raw_complete + reconciliation | `deriveRawComplete`, `VerifyCaptureReconciliation` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestDerivesRawComplete`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\n41|| 13.14.1 unknown blocks maximal_safe | `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\n42|| 13.14.1 Capture Source Basis union | `DecodeSourceBasis`, `buildSourceBasis` | `TestSourceBasisRefusals` |\n43|| 13.14.1 Capture Boundary union, stable proof coupling | `DecodeCaptureBoundary`, `buildBoundary`, `checkProofCoupling` | `TestBoundaryRefusals`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n44|| 13.14.1 unstable is core-created, G2 rejects | `buildBoundary` (Core), `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestBoundaryRefusals/build_core-only_unstable`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n45|| 13.14.1 NativeIdentity closed shape | `DecodeNativeIdentity`, `EncodeNativeIdentity` | `TestNativeIdentityRoundTrip`, `TestIdentityRefusals/native_identity` |\n46|| 13.14.1 source_identity_digest terminal digest | `IdentityDigest` | `TestIdentityDigestIsStable`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip` |\n47|| 13.14.1 WorkspaceBinding closed shape, normalized cwd | `DecodeWorkspaceBinding`, `checkCwdRelative` | `TestIdentityRefusals/workspace_binding` |\n48|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session + Actor rules | `BuildCanonicalSession`, `DecodeCanonicalSession` | `TestBuildCanonicalSessionRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalSessionRefusals` |\n49|| 13.14.1 Canonical Event envelope + 26 kinds + visibility | `BuildCanonicalEvent`, `DecodeCanonicalEvent`, `ValidEventKind` | `TestEventKindVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals` |\n50|| 13.14.1 SourceEvidence + RawReference + synthesized coupling | `DecodeSourceEvidence`, `buildSourceEvidence`, `checkEvidenceCoupling` | `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/evidence` |\n51|| 13.14.1 message-like content blocks, 64 KiB inline bound | `checkPayload`, `checkContentBlocks` | `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/build_envelope` (block rows + 64 KiB boundary) |\n52|| 13.14.1 contiguous ordinals from zero | `CheckOrdinalContiguity` | `TestOrdinalContiguity` |\n53|| 13.14.1 immutable generations | `ParseGeneration`, `Generation.Equal`, `CheckDigestsEqual` | `TestGenerationRefusals`, `TestBoundaryRefusals` |\n54|| 13.14.1 reverse-DNS extensions, no normative reference | `encodeExtensions`, `checkExtensions` | contract round trips + `bad extensions` rows in every refusal table |\n55|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor identity + byte-count agreement | `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` | `TestBlobAgreementRefusals`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` row |\n56|| 10.2 no-replace install (fsync + verify + atomic) | `InstallRawBlob` via `localstore.PutBlob` | `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` |\n57|| 7.8 tuple/probe/manifest/discover/inspect reuse | `sessadapter.DecodeTuple` at every `source_environment` | `bad tuple` rows in raw/capture/session/event tables |\n58|| Byte-identical construction | all Build entries | `RoundTrip` tests rebuild and compare bytes |\n59|\n60|## Durability bound\n61|\n62|This package performs no durable write: `InstallRawBlob` delegates\n63|every byte to `localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob` (no-replace install,\n64|fsync, size/digest verification, quarantine on collision). The\n65|landed crash/idempotency evidence for that discipline lives with\n66|`internal/localstore` (`object_store_test.go`,\n67|`object_store_fault_unix_test.go`, projection fault suites);\n68|`TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` proves the delegation end to end\n69|(double install agrees, tampered bytes refuse). No second write\n70|path exists in this package.\n71|\n72|## Stated bounds (sibling scope)\n73|\n74|- Per-kind Canonical Event payload fact registries beyond the\n75|  Section 13.14.1 envelope enforced in `checkPayload` (normalization\n76|  sibling).\n77|- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\n78|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\n79|- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\n80|- Section 7.8 capture-plan/capture/normalize operation wiring\n81|  (stays owned by `sessadapter`); this package owns the contracts\n82|  those operations produce, not the operation frames.\n83|- `internal/traceability` registry bindings and digest re-pin\n84|  (Story FINAL leaf).","final_result":true}}}
