oundary`, `checkProofCoupling` | `TestBoundaryRefusals`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n44|| 13.14.1 unstable is core-created, G2 rejects | `buildBoundary` (Core), `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestBoundaryRefusals/build_core-only_unstable`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n45|| 13.14.1 NativeIdentity closed shape | `DecodeNativeIdentity`, `EncodeNativeIdentity` | `TestNativeIdentityRoundTrip`, `TestIdentityRefusals/native_identity` |\n46|| 13.14.1 source_identity_digest terminal digest | `IdentityDigest` | `TestIdentityDigestIsStable`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip` |\n47|| 13.14.1 WorkspaceBinding closed shape, normalized cwd | `DecodeWorkspaceBinding`, `checkCwdRelative` | `TestIdentityRefusals/workspace_binding` |\n48|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session + Actor rules | `BuildCanonicalSession`, `DecodeCanonicalSession` | `TestBuildCanonicalSessionRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalSessionRefusals` |\n49|| 13.14.1 Canonical Event envelope + 26 kinds + visibility | `BuildCanonicalEvent`, `DecodeCanonicalEvent`, `ValidEventKind` | `TestEventKindVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals` |\n50|| 13.14.1 SourceEvidence + RawReference + synthesized coupling | `DecodeSourceEvidence`, `buildSourceEvidence`, `checkEvidenceCoupling` | `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/evidence` |\n51|| 13.14.1 message-like content blocks, 64 KiB inline bound | `checkPayload`, `checkContentBlocks` | `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/build_envelope` (block rows + 64 KiB boundary) |\n52|| 13.14.1 contiguous ordinals from zero | `CheckOrdinalContiguity` | `TestOrdinalContiguity` |\n53|| 13.14.1 immutable generations | `ParseGeneration`, `Generation.Equal`, `CheckDigestsEqual` | `TestGenerationRefusals`, `TestBoundaryRefusals` |\n54|| 13.14.1 reverse-DNS extensions, no normative reference | `encodeExtensions`, `checkExtensions` | contract round trips + `bad extensions` rows in every refusal table |\n55|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor identity + byte-count agreement | `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` | `TestBlobAgreementRefusals`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` row |\n56|| 10.2 no-replace install (fsync + verify + atomic) | `InstallRawBlob` via `localstore.PutBlob` | `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` |\n57|| 7.8 tuple/probe/manifest/discover/inspect reuse | `sessadapter.DecodeTuple` at every `source_environment` | `bad tuple` rows in raw/capture/session/event tables |\n58|| Byte-identical construction | all Build entries | `RoundTrip` tests rebuild and compare bytes |\n59|\n60|## Durability bound\n61|\n62|This package performs no durable write: `InstallRawBlob` delegates\n63|every byte to `localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob` (no-replace install,\n64|fsync, size/digest verification, quarantine on collision). The\n65|landed crash/idempotency evidence for that discipline lives with\n66|`internal/localstore` (`object_store_test.go`,\n67|`object_store_fault_unix_test.go`, projection fault suites);\n68|`TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` proves the delegation end to end\n69|(double install agrees, tampered bytes refuse). No second write\n70|path exists in this package.\n71|\n72|## Stated bounds (sibling scope)\n73|\n74|- Per-kind Canonical Event payload fact registries beyond the\n75|  Section 13.14.1 envelope enforced in `checkPayload` (normalization\n76|  sibling).\n77|- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\n78|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\n79|- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\n80|- Section 7.8 capture-plan/capture/normalize operation wiring\n81|  (stays owned by `sessadapter`); this package owns the contracts\n82|  those operations produce, not the operation frames.\n83|- `internal/traceability` registry bindings and digest re-pin\n84|  (Story FINAL leaf).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c777","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b07e-1184-7ee2-a636-22f940ee305b"},"sequence":534,"recorded_at":1780531400001063,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8a76739b-7cd3-4623-8bf5-9ad19ff6cfdd","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"8a76739b-7cd3-4623-8bf5-9ad19ff6cfdd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8a76739b-7cd3-4623-8bf5-9ad19ff6cfdd"},"call_id":"call_01a0b080079177bf9aadf80ea8fd20cd","text":"Read text file `internal/clonebundle/doc.go`.\n1|package clonebundle\n2|\n3|// This package implements the Section 13.14.1 clone capture contracts:\n4|// Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (with\n5|// Capture Items, Capture Source Basis, and Capture Boundary), Canonical\n6|// Session 1.0.0, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (with Source Evidence and raw\n7|// references), the NativeIdentity and WorkspaceBinding identities, raw\n8|// evidence descriptor agreement over Section 10.2 Blob Descriptors,\n9|// reverse-DNS extension keys, and immutable source generations.\n10|//\n11|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Sections\n12|// 7.8, 10.2, and 13.14.1 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md).\n13|//\n14|// Every Decode entry validates a closed shape: exact members, bounded\n15|// scalars, closed vocabularies, sorted-unique order, and self-digest\n16|// agreement. Every Build entry constructs the same bytes\n17|// deterministically: identical inputs produce byte-identical outputs,\n18|// and every Build output decodes clean. Refusals name the offending\n19|// member and never admit a partial object.\n20|//\n21|// Reuse, not fork: Environment Tuples decode through\n22|// sessadapter.DecodeTuple, Blob Descriptors verify through\n23|// canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity plus a local claim comparison\n24|// (never the attesting entry, per the provhost no-attestation bound),\n25|// extension keys admit through\n26|// environ.CheckExtensions, and blob bytes install through\n27|// localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob. The canonicaljson closed-shape\n28|// registry keeps its rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape rows for\n29|// these schemas (that table's census pins every row, so replacing\n30|// them would fork ownership); this package is the validating owner\n31|// and says so here and in TRACEABILITY.md.\n32|//\n33|// Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived): per-kind Canonical Event\n34|// payload fact registries beyond the Section 13.14.1 envelope rules\n35|// enforced here; maximal_safe projection gating past the\n36|// raw_complete=false derivation; target-branch (G2) admission beyond\n37|// RefuseUnstableForTarget; capture-plan/capture/normalize adapter\n38|// operation wiring (Section 7.8 bodies stay owned by sessadapter).\n39|// This package performs no durable write itself: blob installation\n40|// delegates to the landed localstore no-replace discipline, and the\n41|// crash/idempotency evidence for that path is cited in\n42|// TRACEABILITY.md.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
