{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb2f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b07e-1184-7ee2-a636-22f940ee305b"},"sequence":1010,"recorded_at":1780531400002015,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"8a76739b-7cd3-4623-8bf5-9ad19ff6cfdd","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"8a76739b-7cd3-4623-8bf5-9ad19ff6cfdd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"8a76739b-7cd3-4623-8bf5-9ad19ff6cfdd"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b088-4c19-7412-b86c-76cbd3e373bf"},"task_id":"01a0b088-4c19-7412-b86c-76cbd3e373bf","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b088-4c19-7412-b86c-76cbd3e373bf","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-34-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff README.md LOGBOOK.md; echo \\\"=== new files ===\\\"; git status --short internal/clonebundle/ | head; find internal/clonebundle -type f | wc -l\",\n  \"description\": \"Review README and LOGBOOK diff\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 43c6d21..fbedee7 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,14 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-17\\n \\n+### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n+\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/clonebundle` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts over the landed owners — Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (Capture Items, Source Basis, Capture Boundary, core-derived `raw_complete`), Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (Source Evidence, raw refs, content blocks), NativeIdentity/WorkspaceBinding, immutable generations — plus Section 10.2 descriptor agreement and no-replace install via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the closed shape. Row-21 exclusion allowlist (`hosttrust` matchers) enforced at raw-entry and capture-item construction with per-class negatives.\\n+- OWNERSHIP: `canonicaljson` keeps its `rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows (that table's census pins every row); this package is the validating owner and reuses `Canonicalize`/`VerifyObjectIdentity` (blobs), `sessadapter.DecodeTuple`, `environ.CheckExtensions`, `scalar`, and `localstore.PutBlob`. No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n+- EVIDENCE: package suite green (82.2% statements), 17 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` proves the localstore delegation (double install agrees, tampered bytes refuse); durability itself is the landed localstore discipline (purity bound for this package: no second write path). README package section added with test commands and no capability claim.\\n+- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): per-kind event payload fact registries past the envelope; `maximal_safe` planning past the refusal gate; G2 admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`; Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- AC: 18 of 18 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n+\\n ### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n - DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n - F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 1f8fc60..ca5639e 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -2383,6 +2383,33 @@ go test ./internal/matjournal -count=1 -cover\\n python3 internal/matjournal/mutant_harness.py\\n ```\\n \\n+## Clone Bundle and Canonical Session Types\\n+\\n+[`internal/clonebundle`](internal/clonebundle) validates and constructs\\n+the Section 13.14.1 clone capture contracts: Clone Raw Object Manifest\\n+1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 with its Capture Items, Capture\\n+Source Basis, and Capture Boundary, Canonical Session 1.0.0 with its\\n+Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 with Source Evidence and raw byte-range\\n+references, the NativeIdentity and WorkspaceBinding identities, and\\n+immutable source generations. Every Build entry produces byte-identical\\n+canonical bytes for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the\\n+closed shape, the class vocabularies, the included/excluded content\\n+rule, the core-derived `raw_complete` reconciliation, the stable-proof\\n+coupling, and the row-21 hosttrust exclusion allowlist. Blob Descriptor\\n+identity and byte-count agreement verify through `canonicaljson`, and\\n+blob bytes install only through the `localstore` no-replace discipline;\\n+the package performs no durable write itself. The clause map in\\n+[`internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`](internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md)\\n+maps every pinned clause to its production entry and test, with the\\n+sibling-owned bounds stated. It adds no `ax` command, no `doctor`\\n+result, and no runtime capability claim.\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1\\n+go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1 -cover\\n+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py\\n+```\\n+\\n ## Crash/Restart Outcome Gate\\n \\n [`internal/crashgate`](internal/crashgate) executes the Section 13.13\\n=== new files ===\\n?? internal/clonebundle/\\n      19\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5293,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1324,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
